---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — Zephyr Flanigan"
  description="Full Stack Engineer based in New York City. Learn more about my work, experience, and interests."
>
  <!-- ===================== MAIN CONTENT ===================== -->
  <main class="flex-1 pt-28 pb-24 px-8 md:px-16 lg:px-32">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">

      <!-- ---- INTRO ---- -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-lg mb-3">Full Stack Engineer</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve leading-tight mb-8">
          Zephyr Flanigan
        </h1>
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-5">
          I'm a full stack engineer based in New York City with a passion for building
          software that is both technically sound and genuinely pleasant to use. I care
          about the details — from a well-structured API to a transition that feels just right.
        </p>
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed">
          This page is where I try to give a more complete picture of who I am beyond
          a résumé — the work I've done, what drives me, and a bit of what I get up to
          outside of a terminal window.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="border-t mb-20" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.3);"></div>

      <!-- ---- WORK ---- -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Work</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve leading-tight mb-8">
          What I build
        </h2>

        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
          My work sits at the intersection of backend systems and frontend craft. I'm most at
          home designing APIs, thinking through data models, and then following the thread all
          the way to the UI layer — making sure the two halves talk to each other cleanly.
        </p>

        <!-- Role block -->
        <div class="mb-10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-2">
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-xl">Senior Software Engineer</h3>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm">2022 — present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
            Placeholder — currently working at a fast-moving product company where I lead
            development on core platform features. Day-to-day this means designing
            service boundaries, reviewing architecture decisions, shipping features, and
            mentoring junior engineers. Stack: TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL, React.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-2">
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-xl">Software Engineer</h3>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm">2020 — 2022</span>
          </div>
          <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
            Placeholder — worked on a small product team building internal tooling and
            customer-facing dashboards. Wore a lot of hats: wrote backend services,
            owned CI/CD pipelines, and helped migrate a legacy codebase to a modern stack.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-10">
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4 mb-2">
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-xl">Engineering Intern</h3>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm">Summer 2019</span>
          </div>
          <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
            Placeholder — first professional engineering role. Contributed to a data
            pipeline project, learned a lot about production systems, and got hooked on
            the feeling of shipping something real.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Skills -->
        <div>
          <p class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Tools &amp; technologies</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">TypeScript</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">Node.js</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">React</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">PostgreSQL</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">Python</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">Docker</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">AWS</span>
            <span class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-sm border rounded-full px-3 py-1" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.4);">Git</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="border-t mb-20" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.3);"></div>

      <!-- ---- PERSONAL ---- -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Personal</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve leading-tight mb-8">
          Outside the terminal
        </h2>

        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          I grew up in New York and still live here — the city is a constant source of
          energy and I can't imagine being anywhere else. When I'm not writing code I'm
          usually either outdoors or buried in something analog.
        </p>

        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Placeholder — I spend a lot of weekends hiking in the Hudson Valley. There's
          something clarifying about a long trail with no notifications. I keep a
          running list of peaks I want to hit and slowly work through it.
        </p>

        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Placeholder — I read a lot, mostly nonfiction: history, science writing, the
          occasional biography. I'm interested in how systems — social, technical,
          biological — emerge, break down, and get rebuilt. It bleeds into how I think
          about software.
        </p>

        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10">
          Placeholder — I also cook more than most people expect from a software engineer.
          There's a logic to a good recipe that scratches the same itch as a clean
          codebase. The feedback loop is just more immediate — and more delicious.
        </p>

        <!-- Values / ways of working -->
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-lg mb-1">Craft over speed</h3>
            <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
              I'd rather take an extra day to do something right than spend two weeks undoing a shortcut. Good software is slow to build and slow to break.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-lg mb-1">Curiosity first</h3>
            <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
              I ask a lot of questions before writing a line of code. Understanding the problem deeply almost always makes the solution simpler.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve text-lg mb-1">Collaboration as default</h3>
            <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-base leading-relaxed">
              The best work I've done has always been with other people. I prefer to pair, review, and discuss openly rather than work in isolation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="border-t mb-20" style="border-color: rgba(184, 144, 140, 0.3);"></div>

      <!-- ---- CONNECT ---- -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-lichen text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Let's talk</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-jakarta font-semibold text-mauve leading-tight mb-6">
          Get in touch
        </h2>
        <p class="font-jetbrains text-clay text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
          I'm always open to interesting conversations — whether that's a new project,
          a role, or just swapping notes on something you're building.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn font-jetbrains text-sand bg-lichen border-lichen rounded-full hover:bg-olive hover:border-olive">Contact me</a>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
  <!-- ==================== END MAIN CONTENT ==================== -->
</Layout>
